think Rung 3 drew the fused edge with one upstream. The foundation names the motion in the plural — two sources can feed one node — so the fusion whole is a program node derived from two distinct read/ lanes at once.
think Designed derive_from_two_reads over a small read_head_len helper (leaned on twice): both source paths must be read/ (NotAReadPath), the destination must not be (NotAProgramPath), the two sources must differ (SameSource — a fusion wants two inputs, not one twice), unpinned refuses LaneUnknown. Fused content = "a=<la> b=<lb>", a pure function of both heads, bounded to max_summary_bytes via bufPrint.
think Proved independence: refresh source A → a=8 b=2 (only the first moved), refresh source B → a=8 b=3 (only the second moved), while the first fused node still recalls a=4 b=2 — referential transparency across a two-input edge, nothing mutating downstream.
obs The J5 fused-edge arc now stands whole: r1 two lanes on one graph · r2 a re-read is an append · r3 one read feeds one program node · r4 two reads fuse into one. The real network fetch remains the one held seam (Keaton's word) — the genuine outward act.
